e is used. Several varieties exist and it has many various culinary uses. Mass-produced commercial cheese sauces are also made by various companies, in both liquid and dry forms. These prepared sauces are used by consumers and restaurants, and commercial formulations are used in the production of various prepared foods, such as macaroni and cheese mixes and frozen meals."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-cheese-sauce"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheese_sauce"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",[["Nachos","dish/nachos"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Tortilla chip","ingredient/tortilla-chip"],["Tortilla chips","ingredient/tortilla-chips"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/3/32/Broccoli_with_cheese_sauce%2C_Holiday_Restaurant%2C_Semarang%2C_2014-06-19.jpg/500px-Broccoli_with_cheese_sauce%2C_Holiday_Restaurant%2C_Semarang%2C_2014-06-19.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Crisco 1492","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Broccoli_with_cheese_sauce%2C_Holiday_Restaurant%2C_Semarang%2C_2014-06-19.jpg"}},"dish/smorgastarta":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/smorgastarta","n":"Smörgåstårta","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 4 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Smörgåstårta, or sandwich cake (Finnish: voileipäkakku; Estonian: võileivatort; Icelandic: brauðterta), is a savoury main dish, not a dessert, of Swedish origin, popular in Sweden, Finland, Estonia, and Iceland, etc. The name is quite literal, with the dish consisting of a cake-like dish, mainly festive, but composed of layers of bread bound with large amounts of sandwich filling and garnish, structurally similar to a layered cream cake, but culinarily more in line with Toast Skagen. When eaten, it is sliced and served like any other cake."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-smorgastarta"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sm%C3%B6rg%C3%A5st%C3%A5rta"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Estonian cuisine","cuisine/estonian-cuisine"],["Finnish cuisine","cuisine/finnish-cuisine"],["Icelandic cuisine","cuisine/icelandic-cuisine"],["Swedish cuisine","cuisine/swedish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Rye bread","ingredient/rye-bread"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Estonian Cuisine","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"estoniancuisine.com","note":"English-language blog dedicated to Estonian home recipes.","url":"https://estoniancuisine.com/about-estonian-food-blog/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Scandicuisine: Swedish recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"scandicuisine.com","note":"Traditional Swedish recipes from Cecilia, a cook from a Finnish-Swedish family on Åland.","url":"https://scandicuisine.com/category/swedish-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Estonian cuisine","links":[["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Egg butter","dish/egg-butter"],["Glögg","dish/glogg"],["Kvass","dish/kvass"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/c/ca/00_Sm%C3%B6rg%C3%A5st%C3%A5rta.jpg/500px-00_Sm%C3%B6rg%C3%A5st%C3%A5rta.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Johan Andersson","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:00_Sm%C3%B6rg%C3%A5st%C3%A5rta.jpg"}},"dish/steak-tartare":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/steak-tartare","n":"Steak tartare","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 7 cuisines","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Steak tartare, or tartar steak, is a French dish of raw ground (minced) beef. It is usually served with onions, capers, parsley or chive, salt, pepper, Worcestershire sauce and other seasonings, often presented separately, to be added to taste. It is commonly served topped with a raw egg yolk. It is similar to Piedmontese battuta al coltello, as well as Levantine kibbeh nayyeh, Ethiopian kitfo, Turkish çiğ köfte, German Mett and Korean yukhoe."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-steak-tartare"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steak_tartare"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"],["Belgian cuisine","cuisine/belgian-cuisine"],["Czech cuisine","cuisine/czech-cuisine"],["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"],["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine"],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Horse meat","ingredient/horse-meat"],["Maggi","ingredient/maggi"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Cook Like Czechs","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cooklikeczechs.com","note":"English-language blog of traditional Czech home recipes by a Czech cook.","url":"https://cooklikeczechs.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Pardon Your French","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"New Caledonia Tourism: Kanak cooking","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newcaledonia.travel","note":"Official tourism board overview of Kanak food, including bougna cooked in an earth oven.","url":"h